messages:
Ava: Hey all — I pushed the first draft of the launch blog to the drive (link: https://drive.redwood.co/launch-draft). Need quick reviews on two things: benchmark wording (claims around 2.5x cost/call) and the webinar CTA + inbound routing. Hoping to lock copy by tomorrow EOD and schedule publish Wed 9am PT.

Priya: on it. I'll focus on the benchmark paragraph first. Can you paste the exact test setup here so I can sanity-check?

Ava: good call. Quick summary: internal microbenchmark vs baseline endpoint under p50 latency load; avg tokens per request ~120; batching and prefix-cache enabled. Result: 2.5x cost reduction on token units vs baseline with similar output quality on our eval set.

Jon: re: claims — can we hedge wording a bit? e.g., "up to 2.5x lower token cost in our benchmarks" instead of absolute statement. Legal usually prefers that.

Lina: +1 to hedging. Also add short note on dataset/metric: what the eval set is and that quality was comparable (links to eval report).

Ava: ok will change to: "up to 2.5x lower token cost in our benchmarks using continuous batching + KV prefix caching (see eval report)." Drafting now.

Marco: for webinar CTA — we should split leads into two flows: 1) attendees who watched live (send follow-up with slide deck + demo signup), 2) registrants who didn't attend (nurture sequence + on-demand replay). That affects HubSpot routing.

Ava: good, Marco — can you paste the HubSpot routing snippets you want? I can add them to the CTA button action.

Marco: sure. Proposed mapping (paste this into the CTA middleware):

```
// CTA routing pseudocode
if (conversion === 'webinar_attend') {
  hubspot.flow = 'webinar-attendees-deck-demo';
  utm_campaign = 'dedicated_launch_live';
} else if (conversion === 'webinar_register_no_show') {
  hubspot.flow = 'nurture-webinar-replay';
  utm_campaign = 'dedicated_launch_replay';
} else {
  hubspot.flow = 'general-inbound';
  utm_campaign = 'dedicated_launch_blog';
}
```

Ava: perfect. I'll add the code block to the CMS CTA settings.

Priya: back to benchmarks — two tiny suggestions: 1) call out that the eval set is a mix of long-form product prompts and short search prompts, 2) show the p50/p95 latency numbers in a small table or bulleted list.

Ava: will add bullets: p50=120ms, p95=420ms for served workload; note that numbers are medians across 10k requests.

Jon: LegalBot — can you run a quick check on the revised "up to" phrasing and the mention of the eval? @LegalBot

LegalBot: Automated check: "up to" phrasing acceptable. Please ensure no customer names or proprietary data in the eval excerpt. Add backlink to full methodology in footnote.

Ava: added the methodology footnote and replaced the snippet that referenced internal customers.

Lina: UX note — make the primary CTA "Register for launch webinar" and secondary CTA "Read technical notes". On mobile the two buttons should stack; add an inline link to the replay under the second paragraph.

Ava: updated CTAs in the draft and added the mobile stacking note.

Marco: for HubSpot, make sure the CTA includes these UTM params so we can segment: utm_source=blog, utm_medium=post, utm_campaign=dedicated_launch_blog. Also tag contacts with source=launch-blog.

Ava: added UTM block to the CMS snippet.

Ava: quick deploy checklist for publish (pinging @PublishBot): 1) final copy in CMS, 2) hero image uploaded to CDN, 3) HubSpot CTA/webhook configured, 4) social assets scheduled. Can you do a smoke deploy at publish time and confirm webhook receipt?

PublishBot: Scheduled smoke-run window accepted for 2026-06-03T16:00:00Z. I will post a confirmation message in this thread once webhook test passes. :robot_face:

Priya: final ask — can someone double-check the hero claim in the 1st paragraph after edits? want to avoid headline overclaim.

Ava: will iterate headline to: "Reduce inference cost while keeping production-grade latency" and put the explicit benchmark in the subhead. Pinging @Jon for a last look after I push edits (next 30m).

Jon: will review in 30. :thumbsup:

PublishBot: smoke webhook OK at 2026-06-03T16:02:12Z — test payload received and routed to hubspot flow `webinar-attendees-deck-demo`.

Jon: looked through final draft — headline + subhead LGTM. Minor nit: change "production-grade" to "production-ready".

Ava: changed. Final copy pushed to CMS. Thanks everyone — will hit publish schedule after Legal signoff confirmed in the doc. :party_parrot:
